IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`

-- scja3-sch2-second-schedule.l4: the Second Schedule (oaths of office).
-- Layer 1, written from the text alone (SCJA1969.txt lines 5716-5782).  Answers seam 18 of PLAN.md; the asking section is s 69(1), in scja2's range.
-- Three oaths, each headed with the office it is the oath of.  The Schedule allocates the oaths by those headings, so an officer who took a different oath
-- of the three has not taken "the appropriate oath of office set out in the Second Schedule" (s 69(1)): JUST FALSE by the headings (fork: the other reading is NOTHING).

§ `Second Schedule: oaths of office`

-- src:5716 | SECOND SCHEDULE
-- src:5718 | Section 69
-- src:5720 | 1. OATH OF OFFICE OF THE REGISTRAR,
-- src:5721 | DEPUTY REGISTRAR OR ASSISTANT REGISTRAR
@ref Second Schedule oath 1 heading (src:5716-5721)
-- src:5745 | 2. OATH OF OFFICE OF AN INTERPRETER
@ref Second Schedule oath 2 heading (src:5745)
-- src:5761 | 3. OATH OF OFFICE OF OTHER OFFICER
-- src:5762 | OF THE SUPREME COURT
@ref Second Schedule oath 3 heading (src:5761-5762)
DECLARE `sch 2 oath` IS ONE OF
    `sch 2 oath 1 the oath of office of the Registrar, Deputy Registrar or Assistant Registrar`
    `sch 2 oath 2 the oath of office of an Interpreter`
    `sch 2 oath 3 the oath of office of other officer of the Supreme Court`
    `sch 2 another oath that the Second Schedule does not set out`

-- Which oath the Schedule's headings allocate to the officer: oath 1 to the three Registrars, oath 2 to an Interpreter, oath 3 to every other officer of the Supreme Court.
GIVEN officer IS A `Officer of the Supreme Court`
GIVETH A `sch 2 oath`
`sch 2 the oath the headings allocate to the officer` MEANS
    CONSIDER officer
    WHEN Registrar THEN `sch 2 oath 1 the oath of office of the Registrar, Deputy Registrar or Assistant Registrar`
    WHEN `Deputy Registrar` THEN `sch 2 oath 1 the oath of office of the Registrar, Deputy Registrar or Assistant Registrar`
    WHEN `Assistant Registrar` THEN `sch 2 oath 1 the oath of office of the Registrar, Deputy Registrar or Assistant Registrar`
    WHEN Interpreter THEN `sch 2 oath 2 the oath of office of an Interpreter`
    OTHERWISE `sch 2 oath 3 the oath of office of other officer of the Supreme Court`

-- src:5716 | SECOND SCHEDULE
-- src:5718 | Section 69
-- src:5720 | 1. OATH OF OFFICE OF THE REGISTRAR,
-- src:5721 | DEPUTY REGISTRAR OR ASSISTANT REGISTRAR
@ref Second Schedule oath 1 heading (src:5716-5721)
-- src:5745 | 2. OATH OF OFFICE OF AN INTERPRETER
@ref Second Schedule oath 2 heading (src:5745)
-- src:5761 | 3. OATH OF OFFICE OF OTHER OFFICER
-- src:5762 | OF THE SUPREME COURT
@ref Second Schedule oath 3 heading (src:5761-5762)
-- Seam 18 of PLAN.md.
GIVEN officer IS A `Officer of the Supreme Court`
      oath IS A `sch 2 oath`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 2 the oath taken is the appropriate oath of office set out in the Second Schedule` MEANS
    CONSIDER oath
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Schedule sets out three oaths, and an oath that it does not set out is not one it allocates to anyone
    WHEN `sch 2 another oath that the Second Schedule does not set out` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE
        IF oath EQUALS `sch 2 the oath the headings allocate to the officer` officer
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the headings "Oath of office of the Registrar, Deputy Registrar or Assistant Registrar", "Oath of office of an Interpreter", "Oath of office of other officer of the Supreme Court"
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The words of each oath, as the Schedule prints them.  The blanks (the name, the office, the place, the day, the languages) are shown as gaps in the text.
-- src:5723 | I, , having been appointed to the office of
-- src:5725 | do solemnly swear (or affirm) that I will
-- src:5727 | faithfully discharge my judicial duties and I will do right to all manner of people
-- src:5729 | after the laws and usages of the Republic of Singapore without fear or favour,
-- src:5738 | affection or ill will to the best of my ability and I will be faithful and bear true
-- src:5739 | allegiance to the Republic of Singapore.
-- src:5741 | Taken and subscribed before me at this day of .
@ref Second Schedule oath 1 (src:5723-5741)
-- src:5747 | I, , having been appointed an Interpreter of
-- src:5749 | the Court do solemnly swear (or affirm) that I will faithfully interpret, translate
-- src:5751 | and transcribe from the language into the English language and
-- src:5753 | from the English language into the language to the best of my
-- src:5755 | knowledge, skill and ability and without fear or favour, affection or ill will.
-- src:5757 | Taken and subscribed before me at this day of .
@ref Second Schedule oath 2 (src:5747-5757)
-- src:5764 | I, , having been appointed to the office of
-- src:5766 | in the Supreme Court do solemnly and sincerely swear (or affirm)
-- src:5768 | that I will not use or exercise my office corruptly during the time that I remain
-- src:5770 | therein, nor will I take or accept by any means whatsoever any fee or reward from
-- src:5772 | any person or persons, but will truly and faithfully and with convenient speed
-- src:5774 | execute the duties assigned to me and will make true and faithful returns as to the
-- src:5776 | manner and time of the execution of all writs, summonses, warrants, orders,
-- src:5778 | notices and other mandatory processes given to me.
-- src:5780 | Taken and subscribed before me at this day of .
@ref Second Schedule oath 3 (src:5764-5780)
GIVEN oath IS A `sch 2 oath`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`sch 2 the words of the oath` MEANS
    CONSIDER oath
    WHEN `sch 2 oath 1 the oath of office of the Registrar, Deputy Registrar or Assistant Registrar` THEN
        JUST "I, , having been appointed to the office of do solemnly swear (or affirm) that I will faithfully discharge my judicial duties and I will do right to all manner of people after the laws and usages of the Republic of Singapore without fear or favour, affection or ill will to the best of my ability and I will be faithful and bear true allegiance to the Republic of Singapore. Taken and subscribed before me at this day of ."
    WHEN `sch 2 oath 2 the oath of office of an Interpreter` THEN
        JUST "I, , having been appointed an Interpreter of the Court do solemnly swear (or affirm) that I will faithfully interpret, translate and transcribe from the language into the English language and from the English language into the language to the best of my knowledge, skill and ability and without fear or favour, affection or ill will. Taken and subscribed before me at this day of ."
    WHEN `sch 2 oath 3 the oath of office of other officer of the Supreme Court` THEN
        JUST "I, , having been appointed to the office of in the Supreme Court do solemnly and sincerely swear (or affirm) that I will not use or exercise my office corruptly during the time that I remain therein, nor will I take or accept by any means whatsoever any fee or reward from any person or persons, but will truly and faithfully and with convenient speed execute the duties assigned to me and will make true and faithful returns as to the manner and time of the execution of all writs, summonses, warrants, orders, notices and other mandatory processes given to me. Taken and subscribed before me at this day of ."
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Schedule sets out no other oath
    OTHERWISE NOTHING
